Package: mhspcarpi
Title: ARPI Treatment Effects by Baseline Risk in Metastatic Prostate Cancer
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Wataru", "Fukuokaya", email = "wfukuokaya@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements a risk model, developed from individual participant
    data of 4 placebo-controlled randomized clinical trials, that predicts the
    4-year risk of all-cause death with placebo plus androgen deprivation
    therapy in patients with metastatic hormone-sensitive prostate cancer. The
    package uses this baseline risk to report pooled estimates of the treatment
    effects of androgen receptor pathway inhibitors on overall survival: the
    difference in 4-year survival probability, the restricted mean survival
    time difference through 4 years, and the hazard ratio.
